                        "source_sense_id": "a244f539-d60e-3c89-b0c5-6f7294745a4c",
                        "target_lang_word": "debaucher",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "debaucher",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "411c0702-95b2-39b3-9e44-10b46056c673",
                                        "entry_id": "f0d3f568-f691-3d44-a496-1cc3e5993ea1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somebody who debauches or corrupts others; a seducer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ef98b0a0-48b8-45f7-83c6-d2020640fa58",
                        "source_entry_id": "802239ab-829d-3802-8115-2accddee95d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "a244f539-d60e-3c89-b0c5-6f7294745a4c",
                        "target_lang_word": "profligate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "profligate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d44a5f70-1495-32d9-9f03-2bf20160fa07",
                                        "entry_id": "4f0f52f0-bed0-30b5-9d00-7847cafb9e7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inclined to waste resources or behave extravagantly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ad6baf2-2c7b-4bc7-9114-4e5435486254",
                                                "sense_id": "d44a5f70-1495-32d9-9f03-2bf20160fa07",
                                                "text": "[H]er Reputation—That—I have no Reaſon to believe is in Queſtion—But then hovv long her profligate Courſe of Pleaſures may make her able to keep it—is a ſhocking Queſtion! and her Preſumption VVhile ſhe keeps it—inſupportable!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9664040c-80a7-4590-a442-8e506c0cc2c2",
                                                "sense_id": "d44a5f70-1495-32d9-9f03-2bf20160fa07",
                                                "text": "His undignified and profligate exile—needy suitor to-day to the only heiress of the royal French blood, and to-morrow to one of the nieces of the Italian adventurer, Mazarin. Utterly neglectful of what he owes to the kingdom which he hopes to regain, Charles has learned but adversity's worst lesson—expediency."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc97806c-20de-4d03-837a-22617986f8a9",
                                                "sense_id": "d44a5f70-1495-32d9-9f03-2bf20160fa07",
                                                "text": "Jay Rodriguez headed over and Dani Osvaldo might have done better with only David De Gea to beat and, as Southampton bordered on the profligate, United were far more ruthless."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31144c1e-3195-4ff5-b970-077ac94de7ca",
                                                "sense_id": "d44a5f70-1495-32d9-9f03-2bf20160fa07",
                                                "text": "This luxury-loving and profligate shell company is registered at a betting shop on the Caledonian Road, an unlovely thoroughfare in North London on which you'd be more likely to find amphetamines than a top-notch lawyer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "962f5e66-7f59-3941-ba59-48c6b67723b4",
                                        "entry_id": "4f0f52f0-bed0-30b5-9d00-7847cafb9e7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Immoral; abandoned to vice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "229fc06a-6781-4caa-afec-504e23bc62d7",
                                                "sense_id": "962f5e66-7f59-3941-ba59-48c6b67723b4",
                                                "text": "Made prostitute and profligate the muse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "011c9855-8867-42be-9b2d-074363809fae",
                                                "sense_id": "962f5e66-7f59-3941-ba59-48c6b67723b4",
                                                "text": "Time ſenſibly all things impairs; / Our fathers have been worſe than theirs; / And we than ours; next age will ſee / A race more profligate than we / (With all the pains we take) have ſkill enough to be."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45fbf4ed-d0e2-31b4-868d-ad92140e61e2",
                                        "entry_id": "4f0f52f0-bed0-30b5-9d00-7847cafb9e7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Profligated: routed, overcome, driven away."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "as a participle"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b31a894-1a69-4017-bad1-c33134a44d62",
                                                "sense_id": "45fbf4ed-d0e2-31b4-868d-ad92140e61e2",
                                                "text": "By whiche onely policie, the kynges armie was profligate and dispersed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75f90a16-b8c1-4cee-b2eb-9b5f9abafe3d",
                                                "sense_id": "45fbf4ed-d0e2-31b4-868d-ad92140e61e2",
                                                "text": "The Canon laws […] with their Author, are profligate out of this realm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55acb5ea-9f74-3c73-8e69-a22976ff1253",
                                        "entry_id": "4f0f52f0-bed0-30b5-9d00-7847cafb9e7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Overthrown, ruined."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "as a participial adjective"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0dedcc40-e9e1-4e94-b882-630cd9244d08",
                                                "sense_id": "55acb5ea-9f74-3c73-8e69-a22976ff1253",
                                                "text": "The foe is profligate, and run."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "profligate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc40ffa8-1905-3b95-936e-938e17c30776",
                                        "entry_id": "e088c402-e4a9-3abc-a5a8-d5ec597be6a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An abandoned person; one openly and shamelessly vicious; a dissolute person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f7a1922-57a2-45b3-84b3-134f6646942e",
                                                "sense_id": "cc40ffa8-1905-3b95-936e-938e17c30776",
                                                "text": "Have you come to Nelson seeking your death, profligate?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2b6918a-1128-33b0-b509-5da775cbe915",
                                        "entry_id": "e088c402-e4a9-3abc-a5a8-d5ec597be6a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An overly wasteful or extravagant individual."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fe00c6b-0aec-4a80-b54a-6376bf545d60",
                                                "sense_id": "e2b6918a-1128-33b0-b509-5da775cbe915",
                                                "text": "He proposed to call witnesses to show how the prisoner, a profligate and spendthrift, had been at the end of his financial tether, and had also been carrying on an intrigue with a certain Mrs. Raikes, a neighbouring farmer’s wife."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "profligate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf581dd0-d5de-3ca6-aa10-1903c357e7d1",
                                        "entry_id": "90f00e22-5533-388f-8b2d-e10b071dee53",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drive away; to overcome."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55b00dd1-b045-4b70-8a0e-fea248413f13",
                                                "sense_id": "cf581dd0-d5de-3ca6-aa10-1903c357e7d1",
                                                "text": "Such a stipulation would remove one powerful temptation to profligate pennyless seducers, of whom there are too many prowling in the higher circles ;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7ee320a7-3636-4d08-983e-84d47d3a0af1",
                        "source_entry_id": "802239ab-829d-3802-8115-2accddee95d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "a244f539-d60e-3c89-b0c5-6f7294745a4c",
